WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.667
-I'm so happy you're here.
-Thanks for having me, man.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.634
-I'm a fan of yours.
It's so nice to meet you here.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.033
And I was very excited to meet
your mother, as well, backstage.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.634
-My mom is here. Hi, Mom.
-Where is mom?

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.300
Is mom in the audience?
-Where is mother?

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.501
-There's ma. Hey, mom!

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.634
-Oh, don't pretend like
you're not here.

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:15.634
Hi, Mom. -I know.

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:16.767
It's like,
"Don't put me on camera.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:18.133
Don't put me on camera."

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:19.501
-She's like, "Don't do it.
That's your job, not mine."

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:22.467
-Mom, you got to be very proud,
very proud of your --

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:25.300
Does your mom get to -- Does she
get to see you perform a lot?

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.200
-She's actually -- She came for
the first time last --

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.601
this past season?

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:31.601
Yeah. So that was the first time
she saw me employed as an actor,

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:33.467
which is cool, 'cause I'm like,
"Mom, I have a job.

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:36.367
-Mom, things are going pretty
well for this guy, yeah.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.334
I've got to say,
the new season just came out,

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:41.067
and it is the
number-1 show on Netflix.

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:42.334
I mean, is that after --

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:45.467
Immediately after
the release on Thursday.

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:47.534
Congrats on that.

00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:50.067
In fact, a lot of fans have
already finished

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.334
the whole third season,
if that's even possible.

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:53.601
-How?
-Wait.

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:54.834
Someone is waving her hand.
You finished it all?

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:56.701
-You finished it?
-How? When?

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:57.801
-Are you okay?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.934
-No, I mean,
where did you find the --

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:04.033
-I started it Friday night
and finished it Saturday night.

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:07.133
-So you marathoned?
That's a lot of hours.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:10.467
And what -- Unbiased,
what is your review of the show?

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:11.767
Clearly, you liked it.

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:14.934
-It's the best season.
-Whoa! It's the best season.

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:16.801
That's what you want.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:18.534
-I will Venmo you later.
-That's not paid advertisement.

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:19.834
-I'll get her Venmo.

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:24.133
-Oh, yeah, you'll get her --
Yeah, her Venmo, yeah.

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:27.734
Besides these great fans
that you have for the show --

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.667
'Cause, man,
you got a giant fan base.

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:30.701
They really support you.

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:31.834
How about celebrity fans?

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:33.267
Anyone ever shock you
where you're like,

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:34.901
"Oh, my gosh,
they watch the show?"

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:37.968
-Yeah, yeah.
We've had some interesting ones.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:41.467
I think the funniest one --
I grew up in Orlando,

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:42.968
so I'm a huge Orlando Magic fan.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:44.133
-Yeah.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:47.834
-And I got to FaceTime with
Shaquille O'Neal.

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:51.334
And so, you know, I got the,
"Hey, man, hey, how are you?"

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:52.434
-Whoa. Wow. That's a --

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:54.334
-"Congratulations on
the show, man.

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:55.467
Congratulations.
We really like --"

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:57.033
-"What's happening
with this new season?"

00:01:57.033 --> 00:02:00.467
-"Can you spoil anything?"
"Sorry, Shaq. Can't do that."

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.000
-I love everyone's
FaceTiming each other.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.968
No one does that with me.
It's very funny.

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:05.000
-I'll FaceTime you.
-Yeah. You will?

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.033
-Yeah.

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.667
-You're a very funny
human being.

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.267
We were talking backstage,
and I was saying,

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.767
"What's it like shooting this
in the jungle?"

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:15.367
And very interesting stories of
shooting in the jungle

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.634
that I didn't even think about.

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.701
But can you just run through
maybe two or three?

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:22.100
-Sure. Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.868
So, this show,
it takes a lot of effort,

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:28.267
physical effort, exertion.

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:29.868
So, we shot in Barbados
this year.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:33.734
And we were in the jungle for
an extended period of time.

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.934
And there was one day in
particular where the universe

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:38.434
just decided to not work
in my favor.

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:40.467
-But -- Why not, though?
I think it's good.

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:42.100
-Sure, yeah, no.
-People need to know this.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.667
-So, there's a stunt
that happens

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:46.501
at the end of the final episode.

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:47.901
Spoiler alert.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.868
-Yeah. I looked right at you.
Don't spoil. Yeah.

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.801
-I'm not going to do it.
Don't do it.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.200
But, anyways, that happens.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.400
And it was
a very exhausting stunt.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.200
So I'm leaning against a tree,

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.133
and next thing you know,
my arm is on fire.

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:01.467
And I'm like,
"What is going on?"

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:03.701
So, one of our Bajan crew
members looked at me and says,

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:05.767
"That's poison tree sap,
and that's all over your arm."

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:08.200
So I'm like,
"Oh, that's awesome."

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.501
-Poison tree sap?
-Yeah.

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.901
So, they put me in a van
and they started

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:14.033
putting ointments on me
that I have no idea what it is,

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:15.667
but I'm just kind of
going with the flow.

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:18.133
So, I recover from that,
and I'm talking to my director

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.634
sort of like, "I think I'm okay.

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:22.334
I have a pulse. I'm not dying."

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:24.267
And I feel something hit me
in the back of the head.

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:25.434
And he's looking at me like --

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:29.567
-This is a real story.
-This is 100% true.

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:30.601
-Like a smack.

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:32.767
-It was a full-on, like...

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:36.734
Jerked my body forward.
And I was like, "What --"

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:38.367
-"What was that?"
-And he goes, "Bird.

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:39.767
That was a bird.

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:42.367
A bird just -- A bird flew into
the back of your head."

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:44.734
-See, that made me laugh
there 'cause --

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:48.434
So, a bird attacks you
after the poison tree sap.

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:50.133
Yeah. And then a bird
dive-bombs your head.

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:51.400
-Yep.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.167
-And you go, "Oh, my God.
Well, that's it. Go home."

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.267
-I'm just trying to make
a TV show.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.701
-Hey, man, just trying to
entertain people.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:56.934
-Yeah.

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.133
-And then you go,
"Well, let's do another take.

00:03:58.133 --> 00:03:59.267
I'm good.

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:01.167
Let's just enjoy
being in the jungle."

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:03.467
-Yeah, the jungle.
It's just so great.

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:05.601
It's a lovely place.
Highly recommend it.

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:07.701
-Yeah. And you're there.
You're in nature.

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:09.334
It's beautiful.
-So beautiful.

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:12.334
So humid. So, so humid.

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:13.767
-It starts to rain.

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:16.334
-And, so, it starts to rain,
says one of our crew members.

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:17.501
He looks at me and he goes,
"Oh, thank God.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:19.767
It's raining finally.
This will cool us down."

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:22.033
So, I'm like,
"Oh, wow. It's raining."

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:26.567
And I look up, and, immediately,
he says, "Nope, not rain.

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:29.067
That's monkeys peeing."

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:32.634
And a monkey --
a monkey literally pees

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:35.334
directly in my eyeball.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:38.400
A monkey peed in my eyeball.
So, um...

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.667
-That's a great day at work.

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:41.834
-Yeah, so,
I got poison tree sap,

00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:43.367
a bird flew into
the back of my head,

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:46.467
and a monkey pissed
on my eyeball, so...

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:49.133
-And you still look like this.
I mean, look at this guy.

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:51.200
Come on. It's a nip slip!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.567
-It's a -- Yeah.
-Yeah, you missed --

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:53.701
-Yeah, we should blur that out.

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:54.934
-Yeah, you missed
one of the buttons.

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:56.100
-Yeah, oopsie-poopsie.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.367
-Missed one of
the buttons on there, yeah.

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:59.367
-I think it's lopsided, too.
I think I got to --

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:02.868
-Yeah, you missed a few buttons
when you put the shirt on.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.167
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:06.033
Here's Chase Stokes in
"Outer Banks."

00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:07.567
Take a look at this.

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:10.234
-That's exactly what my dad
would do to call me home.

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:13.133
Sarah, that -- that pattern,
those bells.

00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:17.467
[ Bells ringing ]
The ding...ding...ding-ding.

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:20.701
Sarah, that --
that's him calling me home.

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.767
-I know -- It -- Yeah.

00:05:22.767 --> 00:05:27.634
It -- That's --
It's really weird.

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:28.667
But it's not him.

00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:30.133
-Okay, how do --
how do you know that?

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:31.267
-You know why.
-No.

00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:32.267
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.
-I'm sorry.

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:33.367
-No, no, listen.

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:34.767
Maybe -- maybe
you get beaten enough,

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.567
you aren't able to see the
miracle right in front of you.

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:39.267
I mean, that's exactly how he
used to call me home.

00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:40.501
Maybe it is him.

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:42.167
Maybe the universe
is trying to give me a gift,

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:43.167
and we're not even --

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:45.133
-Okay.
-What?

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:47.100
-Okay. I get it.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.934
You want to go to the tower
to go look?

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:51.200
Go look, okay?

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.767
-Yeah.
Chase Stokes, everybody.

00:05:53.767 --> 00:05:58.100
Season 3 of "Outer Banks"
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.901
We'll be right back with
Micky Dolenz.

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:01.133
Stick around, everybody.

